# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# This is the BUILD CONTEXT, not the image. `cloudbuild.yaml` runs the
# test suite as build step 0, so tests/, pytest.ini and
# requirements-dev.txt MUST be uploaded — excluding them here made the
# first build fail with "Could not open requirements file:
# requirements-dev.txt".
#
# Keeping tests and reference material OUT OF THE IMAGE is
# `.dockerignore`'s job, and it does exactly that. The shell spec's
# instruction to exclude resources/, tests/ and docs/ assumes a
# source-based deploy where the upload becomes the image; with a
# cloudbuild.yaml that tests before it builds, the two lists differ.
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
.venv.nosync/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
